[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Caro-Kann Defence"]
[Variation "Advance Variation, Bayonet Attack"]
[ECO "B12"]
[Character "solid"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "bishop-retreat,c5-break"]
[For "black"]
[Kind "rare"]
[Opponent "4.g4"]
[Start "short-system 3...Bf5"]

4. g4 $6 { White attacks the bishop at once, but the pawn on g4 now has nothing behind it, and the squares f3 and h3 are weak. } 4... Bd7 { The simple retreat. White has spent a move and weakened the kingside, so Black can calmly start the fight in the centre. } 5. Be3 ( 5. Nc3 e6 6. Be3 h5 7. gxh5 c5 ) ( 5. h4 e6 6. Nf3 c5 7. Be3 Nc6 ) 5... e6 { Supports d5 and prepares the usual ...c5 break. } 6. Nf3 c5 { Attacks d4 before White can complete development. } 7. dxc5 Qc7 { Attacks the pawn on e5 and the one on c5 at once, so Black wins a pawn back. If White varies, aim at d4 with ...c5 and ...Nc6, and use ...h5 to attack the loose g4 pawn. } *
